  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 154 PM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nAfter moving over our area this weekend, the upper-level ridge sets \nup over eastern portions of the CONUS by early next week. As a \nresult, west Texas and southeast New Mexico will generally remain on \nthe western fringe of the ridge. This will continue to promote above \nnormal temperatures across the region through the forecast period. \nHighs top out in the upper 90s for most locations, and temperatures \nat/above 100 degrees will mainly be found in and around the river \nvalleys. Lows bottom out in the low-to-mid 70s, with 60s in the \nhigher terrain. Most of the area is expected to remain dry through \nnext week as well. The \"best\" rain chances (10-20%) will be in and \naround the western higher terrain, mainly the product of upslope \nflow and disturbances rounding the ridge.\n\nSprang",
